 success←old ReplaceFolderBy new;temp;flag;qdmx;msg;rc;hinted
⍝ Performs the following actions:
⍝ * Establish a temp name dynamically
⍝ * Rename "old" to "temp"
⍝ * Re-create the folder "old"
⍝ * Copy the contents of "new" into "old"
⍝ * Delete "new"
⍝ * Delete "temp"
 temp←'-'{~⎕NEXISTS n←⍺{(1⊃⍵),⍺,(2⊃⍵)}⎕NPARTS ⍵:n ⋄ (⍺,⍺)∇ ⍵}{⍵↓⍨-(¯1↑⍵)∊'/\'}old
 flag←0
 hinted←0
 :Repeat
     :Trap 19 22
         temp(⎕NMOVE F.ExecNfunction)old
         flag←1
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
⍝ `Message` is what tells the cases apart, and without it this question cannot be answered sensibly:
⍝ "Access is denied" is a permission problem and retrying is pointless, while "used by another
⍝ process" means something holds a handle - and under Windows a single open file anywhere inside the
⍝ folder is enough to stop the folder itself from being renamed.
         :If ~hinted
⍝ Said once, and before the first question, because otherwise the only way out is to keep saying
⍝ "yes" to a question that cannot become answerable by itself.
             1 PrintToSession'*** A folder cannot be renamed while anything holds something inside it.'
             1 PrintToSession'    A file manager, an editor or a command shell will do it, and it need not be'
             1 PrintToSession'    showing the folder now: a handle left over from an earlier visit is enough,'
             1 PrintToSession'    so checking the open tabs proves nothing. Windows calls it "Access is denied".'
             1 PrintToSession'    Sysinternals'' "handle.exe <folder>" names the process that holds it.'
             hinted←1
         :EndIf
         msg←'Attempt to replace ',old,' resulted in a ',qdmx.EM,' error'
         msg,←((0<≢qdmx.Message)/': ',qdmx.Message),'; try again?'
         :If ~YesOrNo msg
             'Cancelled by user after error'⎕SIGNAL 98
         :EndIf
     :EndTrap
 :Until flag
 F.MkDir old
 :Trap 0
     old(⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)F.ExecNfunction)new,'/*'
     {}F.RmDirByForce new
     success←1
 :Else                      ⍝ Roll back
     {}F.RmDirByForce old
     F.MkDir old
     old(⎕NMOVE⍠('Wildcard' 1)F.ExecNfunction)temp,'/*'
     success←0
 :EndTrap
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce temp
 :If rc≠0
     ⍞←'*** Warning: removing ',temp,' failed but the re-install worked!',⎕UCS 10   ⍝Note: this has failed a number of times, and we don't know why
 :EndIf
